# Auto-detect text files, perform LF normalization
* text=auto eol=lf

# Explicit text files
*.ts text
*.js text
*.json text
*.md text
*.yml text
*.yaml text
*.toml text

# Binary files
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.woff2 binary

# Generated — exclude from GitHub language stats and diff spam
data/** linguist-generated=true
pnpm-lock.yaml linguist-generated=true merge=binary

# Every PR appends its entry directly under `## [Unreleased]`, so any two of
# them touch the same lines and collide. With ~30 PRs open at once that was
# the single largest source of merge conflicts, and resolving it is always the
# same mechanical act: keep both entries.
#
# `merge=union` does exactly that — git concatenates both sides of the
# conflicting hunk instead of stopping. Safe here because changelog entries are
# append-only and independent; it would be wrong for a file where the two sides
# could contradict each other.
#
# One follow-up is needed after a union resolution: the concatenation does not
# leave a blank line between the joined entries, which trips markdownlint
# MD022/MD032. Run `pnpm exec markdownlint-cli2 --fix CHANGELOG.md` and commit
# — it is a pure whitespace fix, verified to change nothing else.
CHANGELOG.md merge=union
